# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Room / identity (read this)
#
# The long hex in the `join` URL path is your room invite token (like a
# password). Whoever has this file—or the URL—can join that relay room. A
# separate 6-digit code is NOT required by Meshcore for that link; the token
# already authenticates the invite. If you want a simple human check between
# teammates, agree on a 6-digit "coordination PIN" out-of-band (Signal, in
# person) and say it once after joining—do NOT put a real PIN in git.
#
# "Master" / room setup: only the relay UI (or whoever operates fly.dev) can
# create or own a room. Cursor/IDE agents do not keep a live Meshcore session;
# you (or an operator) open the join URL, then paste instructions for others.
#
# If this repo is public or shared widely: rotate the join link on the relay,
# remove the old URL from git history, and prefer a private copy of this file
# (e.g. `.meshkore.local` gitignored + `.meshkore.example` in-repo without token).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# hyverk incremental KV (2026-04-15) — tell other agents to pull this repo
# Coordinator + all GPU nodes must deploy together (new WS message types).
# Python nodes need recent transformers (DynamicCache + create_causal_mask).
# See _rjj/log/AUDIT-distributed-inference.md for context.

# --- post-push: paste into Meshcore / team channel for other agents ---
# REPO: asimovia/hiverk (pull latest main or your integration branch)
# ALL-AT-ONCE: deploy coordinator + every GPU inference node on the same commit.
# BUILD: cargo build -p hyverk-coordinator -p hyverk-node (needs protoc for hyverk-proto)
# PYTHON: pip install -U "transformers>=4.45" torch ; restart node_forward serve on :18100
# CHECK: server stdout JSON must include "kv_incremental": true after load
# TEST: POST /api/v1/ws-inference with prompt + max_tokens>=8 ; compare tokens_per_sec vs prior commit
